.TH TELACHAT 1 "2026-05-26" "Telachat 0.56.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
telachat \- local CLI and desktop chat client for OpenAI-compatible APIs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B telachat
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Telachat
is a local chat client with a CLI, GTK frontend, and Tk frontend. It stores chat
history in SQLite, supports provider/model profiles, per-session model metadata,
prompt templates, folders, folder system prompts, per-session tags, soft
archives, session forking, user-message editing, regeneration, and Markdown
exports.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create the default configuration.
.TP
.B profiles
Show configured provider profiles with redacted API keys. The default config
includes non-default local presets for LM Studio, Ollama, and Jan. Use
\fB--json\fR for structured output.
.TP
.B models
Show configured model IDs per profile without network access. Use
\fB--live\fR with \fB--profile NAME\fR to query the selected provider's
\fB/models\fR endpoint. Use \fB--json\fR for structured output.
.TP
.B config-check, config
Check local configuration, model metadata, and secret references without an API
request. Use \fB--profile NAME\fR to check one profile. Use \fB--strict\fR to
fail when checked non-Codex provider secret sources are missing. Use
\fB--json\fR for redacted structured output. The output also reports whether
global profile-header validation is enabled.
.TP
.B theme
Show or set the persistent GUI theme. Supported themes are \fIsystem\fR,
\fIlight\fR, \fIdark\fR, \fIhigh-contrast\fR, \fIsolarized-light\fR,
\fIsolarized-dark\fR, \fInord\fR, \fIdracula\fR, \fIgruvbox\fR, \fIocean\fR,
\fIforest\fR, \fIrose\fR, \fIgraphite-glass\fR, \fIliquid-chrome\fR,
\fIblack-ice\fR, and \fIbrushed-steel\fR. The environment variable \fBTELACHAT_THEME\fR
overrides the config for one process; \fBTELACHAT_SYSTEM_THEME\fR only fixes
system-palette detection for one process.
The same setting can be changed inside interactive chat with \fB/theme NAME\fR.
.TP
.B templates
List configured prompt templates. Templates support \fB{input}\fR,
\fB{date}\fR, \fB{time}\fR, and \fB{datetime}\fR. Use \fB--json\fR for a
structured template inventory with preview, size, and variable metadata.
.TP
.B folders
List or manage chat folders, folder-level system prompts, and optional
folder-level backend defaults. Use \fB--set-backend FOLDER PROFILE [MODEL]\fR
or \fB--clear-backend FOLDER\fR for provider/model defaults. Use \fB--json\fR
for structured output; system prompts are included only with \fB--show-system\fR.
.TP
.B ask
Send a single prompt. Use \fB--json\fR for a structured one-shot response with
profile, model, and token usage when the provider reports it.
.TP
.B chat
Start an interactive CLI chat.
.TP
.B sessions
List active saved sessions with optional search, folder filtering, tag
filtering, archive filtering, and sorting. Session search also matches saved
provider/model/tag metadata. Use \fB--archived\fR for only archived chats,
\fB--all\fR for active plus archived chats, and \fB--json\fR for structured
output.
.TP
.B stats
Show local history inventory without message content. Counts sessions,
messages, folders, tags, profiles, models, and stored provider token usage
when available. Use \fB--json\fR for structured output.
.TP
.B context
Estimate one session's next-request context size without message content.
Reports stored/request messages, character counts, and approximate tokens. Use
\fB--json\fR for structured output.
.TP
.B archive
Hide one session from normal session lists without deleting it.
.TP
.B unarchive
Restore one archived session to normal session lists.
.TP
.B tags
List tag counts or manage tags for one session. Use \fB--add TAG\fR,
\fB--remove TAG\fR, \fB--set TAG...\fR, \fB--clear\fR, and \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B fork
Copy a saved session into a new independent chat.
.TP
.B export
Export one session as Markdown. Use \fB--json\fR for structured output with
session metadata and ordered messages.
.TP
.B import-session
Import one \fBtelachat.session.v1\fR JSON export additively as a new session.
Use \fB--title\fR, \fB--folder\fR, and \fB--json\fR for import metadata and
structured output. Use \fB--dry-run\fR to validate and count without writing.
.TP
.B export-folder
Export a selected folder as Markdown files, a single bundled Markdown file, or
machine-readable JSON with \fB--json\fR. By default only active sessions are
exported; use \fB--archived\fR or \fB--all\fR to include archived chats.
.TP
.B import-folder
Import one \fBtelachat.folder.v1\fR JSON export additively. Use
\fB--folder\fR to choose a target folder and \fB--json\fR for structured output.
Use \fB--dry-run\fR to validate and count without writing.
.TP
.B backup
Create a local ZIP backup containing a consistent SQLite history copy,
\fIconfig.redacted.toml\fR, and \fImanifest.json\fR. Raw API keys and envfiles are
not included.
.TP
.B packaging/linux/install-telachat.sh
When run from a source checkout or release bundle, install the zipapp, launchers,
manpages, Freedesktop desktop entry, icon, and optional desktop shortcut under a
configurable Linux prefix.
.TP
.B restore, import-backup
Import the history from a Telachat backup ZIP into the existing SQLite database.
Existing sessions are not overwritten; imported sessions receive new IDs. Use
\fB--dry-run\fR to show counts without importing.
.TP
.B doctor
Check profile configuration and the configured API. Use \fB--json\fR for
redacted structured output.
.TP
.B skill-watchdog
Compact oversized Codex Skill frontmatter descriptions to a loader-compatible
length while preserving the Skill body. Use \fB--json\fR for structured output.
.TP
.B gtk, gui
Start the GTK desktop frontend.
.TP
.B tk
Start the Tk desktop frontend.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
telachat doctor --chat
telachat --version
telachat models
telachat models --live -p huggingface --json
telachat config-check
telachat config-check --strict
telachat config-check --profile huggingface --strict
telachat config-check --json
telachat doctor --json --chat
telachat skill-watchdog --json
telachat theme dark
telachat chat
/theme dracula
telachat ask -p huggingface -m TKI "Hallo"
telachat ask -p openai -m gpt-5.5 --reasoning-effort high "Hallo"
telachat ask --json "Hallo"
telachat templates
telachat templates --json
telachat ask --template summarize "Langer Text"
telachat folders --create Arbeit --system "Antworte projektbezogen."
telachat folders --set-backend Arbeit huggingface TKI
telachat sessions --json
telachat stats --json
telachat context SESSION_ID --json
telachat sessions --tag projekt
telachat sessions --archived
telachat sessions --all
telachat archive SESSION_ID
telachat unarchive SESSION_ID
telachat tags SESSION_ID --add projekt --add review
telachat fork SESSION_ID --title "Variante A"
telachat export SESSION_ID --json
telachat import-session session.json --folder Importe
telachat export-folder Arbeit -o ./arbeit-export
telachat export-folder Arbeit --single-file -o arbeit.md
telachat export-folder Arbeit --json -o arbeit.json
telachat import-folder arbeit.json --folder Importiert
telachat import-folder arbeit.json --dry-run --json
telachat backup -o ./backups
telachat restore --dry-run ./backups/telachat-backup.zip
telachat-tk
telachat-gtk
.fi
.SH SLASH COMMANDS
Interactive CLI chat and both GUIs understand slash commands in the prompt.
The CLI uses Readline Tab completion for commands and context values when
available. The GUI prompt shows command suggestions while typing and Tab
completes the current command.
.PP
.nf
/help
/new [Titel]
/rename TITLE
/delete
/pin
/unpin
/archive
/unarchive
/archives
/tag TAG [TAG...]
/untag TAG [TAG...]
/tags [SESSION]
/stats
/context
/doctor
/edit-last TEXT
/fork [TITLE]
/regen
/templates
/template NAME TEXT
/folder NAME
/folder-system TEXT
/rename-folder NAME
/delete-folder
/move NAME
/unfile
/sort newest|oldest|title|title-desc|provider
/search TEXT
/find TEXT
/provider NAME
/model NAME
/models [live]
/permissions
/left
/system [prompt]
/sessions
/load ID
/profile [name]
/profiles
/history [n]
/export [datei.md]
/exit
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/telachat/config.toml
Default configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/telachat/history.sqlite3
SQLite chat history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/telachat/*.env
Recommended location for local API-key envfiles. Keep these files private.
.SH SECURITY
Do not store real API tokens in the repository, Wiki, or Gists. Prefer
\fBenv:NAME\fR or \fBenvfile:/path#NAME\fR references in configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR telachat-tk (1),
.BR telachat-gtk (1)
